    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature for owners: the request may include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and responses expose `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nFollowing the project's established pattern for owner fields (editable input fields live on `OwnerFields`, derived read-only fields are computed by `@Transient` getters on the `Owner` entity and carried onto the DTO by MapStruct), I made these changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `title` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (so it's accepted on input and returned), and a read-only `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`) are generated from this at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter, plus a derived `@Transient getSalutation()` that returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is null/blank.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `title` column so it survives the POST\u2192GET round trip. Tests run against `hsqldb`.\n\nThe existing `OwnerMapper` required no changes: `title` maps by name automatically in both directions, and `salutation` maps automatically from the new getter onto the DTO.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreComposesSalutation`, which POSTs `title=DR`/`lastName=who` then asserts `$.salutation == \"DR who\"` on GET) passes, and the full suite is green.",
