    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- `getSalutation()` lives in the right unit: it's a pure derivation over `title` + `lastName`, placed on the `Owner` entity alongside the existing derived, `@Transient` display getters (`getInitials()`-style method directly above it, `getTelephoneDisplay()` directly below). It follows that established convention exactly \u2014 same `@Transient` annotation, same Javadoc style cross-referencing the source getters and stating \"not persisted.\"\n- The new `title` field, its getter/setter, and column are placed consistently with the sibling `email` field (field grouped with the other columns, accessors in the same order).\n- The schema change is applied uniformly across all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) with a consistent `VARCHAR(10)`, matching how `email`/`customer_code` are mirrored across them \u2014 no dialect left behind.\n- The OpenAPI additions mirror existing property docs (title/description/example, and `readOnly: true` on the derived `salutation` just like `telephoneDisplay`).\n\nNothing is duplicated, no class or method is becoming a catch-all, and a maintainer would find this a natural extension of the existing derived-property pattern.",
